# steps/named-struct-exec.md, slice 1 (plan §3 :245 (a)): a named Structure closed by `end: Counter`
# whose body holds statements besides its field -- an assignment to it and a bare `return` (Q19.2 = 2,
# "the whole body, as a method's").  Construction computes the initializer (book :928) and runs no
# statement: Counter\n reads 4, not 5.  Before, the body took field declarations only ("a Structure
# reference field needs a name").  Entry 7.
Counter:
    size_t: n 4U
    n: n + 1U
    return
end: Counter
size_t: got 0U
got: Counter\n
int: ok 0
if: got = 4U
    ok: 7
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: ok; stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
